# Test temp files (NOT *_test.go — those are real Go tests we ship)
#
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. Unanchored, "testing/" matched ANY directory
# of that name at any depth, and the only one in the tree is docs/testing/ — so the
# pattern protected nothing and silently ignored committed documentation. TEST_PLAN.md
# and GITLAB_CI_TESTING_TRACKER.md are tracked only because they predate it; a NEW
# file added there was invisible to `git add` and would have been dropped from its PR
# without a word (caught while adding docs/testing/SCORE_CORPUS.md).
/testing/
tmp/
temp/
*_mock.go
mock_*.go
*_stub.go
stub_*.go
*.bench
benchmark*.txt
benchmark*.out
benchmark*.log
benchmark_results*
*.prof*
profile.out

